UNAOS_NOSDWRITE   NA   --evidence: sdwrite 24 sites 21 Pi-live 1 NEG. DELIBERATELY absent from K8_FEATS, and the Pi-live count is the reason rather than an oversight. `sdwrite` (A60, DEFAULT ON in the general knob map) lifts the TegraSd write veto; its tegra-gated half cannot reach a Pi image at all, but its OTHER half is the arch-neutral posture FORWARD at fs/vfs.rs:1805 and fs/bootdisk.rs:1372 — `NativeBackend::write_veto` stops asserting `None` and forwards the block layer's answer for the handle the shared unafs mount rides. On the Pi that handle is `Global`, so arming this knob on kernel8 would make `/`'s `rw=` (and the shell's pre-mutation refusal) follow FRGUARD's `default_writable()` instead of a flat yes. That is arguably more honest and it is a CHANGE TO THE PI'S BEHAVIOUR, which is the pi seat's call and not this arc's (R39: no seat proofs another seat's board; orin cannot run `kernel8-test`). Absent from K8_FEATS the Pi image is byte-identical to baseline and the knob is inert there BY CONSTRUCTION. Registered 2026-09-12 by the SDWRITE2 executor (orin, ledger A60), which names the open question in that row.
