UNAOS_WIFI4   NA   --evidence: wifi4 21 sites, 0 Pi-live, 0 negated [implies: wifi, wifi2, wifi3]. Twenty are `#[cfg(feature = "wifi4")]`/`#[cfg(all(feature = "wifi3", not(feature = "wifi4")))]` attributes in crates/kernel/src/wifi/bringup.rs and the twenty-first is PROSE (the section header quoting its own gate). There is no second file and no arch-neutral consumer: `src/wifi/` is declared `#[cfg(all(feature = "wifi", target_arch = "x86_64"))]` in lib.rs and `bringup.rs` is `#[cfg(feature = "wifi2")]` inside it, so an aarch64 compile never lexes the file — neither the `nvidia-kepler`-in-`video/wm.rs` trap (arch-neutral file) nor the `rastmc` trap (x86-gated callee reached from a Pi-live caller) applies, because there is no aarch64-lexed site of any kind. A K8_FEATS arm would arm nothing. Not merely absent from the Pi image but UNBUILDABLE there as written: the whole arc reaches its device through `arch::pci` config space (cfg:0x80, the bcma BAR0 window selector) and the aarch64 tree provides no config-space accessor; the subject is a PCIe BCM4331 in a 2012 rMBP and there is no such part on a Pi. Same class and same argument as the four wifi rows above, which are TODO only because they predate this file's NA-with-evidence rule. Added 2026-09-17 with the §S5 PHY/radio rung (rmbp-ledger B124).
