UNAOS_KEPLER_KFBIND       NA   --evidence, re-run at this commit and quoted verbatim: `nvidia-kepler-kfbind: 3 site(s), 0 Pi-live, 0 negated  [implies: nvidia-kepler, nvidia-kepler-fifo]` — the `pub mod kepler_fifo` declaration in `drivers/gpu/mod.rs` and the rung's TWO call sites in `drivers/gpu/kepler.rs` (phase A immediately pre-submit, phase B immediately below the DISCRIMINATOR loop); line numbers drift, so re-run `scripts/k8-reach.py --evidence UNAOS_KEPLER_KFBIND` rather than trusting them. ONE live read in the producer, arroyo, writing `_feats` (`nvidia-kepler-kfbind`). THREE INDEPENDENT REASONS, the same three the seven SHUTRESTORE rows above establish for this same file family, with the SECOND strengthened by this feature's extra implication. FIRST: `kernel8()` builds its OWN curated feature list — `local K8_FEATS="baremetal,skip_xhci"`, extended only by its own explicit arms — and NEVER reads the `_feats` knob-mapping block, so a knob that writes `_feats` cannot change a byte of a kernel8 image. Command: `grep -n 'K8_FEATS=' unaos/arroyo` (every assignment is inside kernel8(), none from _feats). SECOND, and it would still hold if the mapping block were ever wired into kernel8: the feature implies BOTH `nvidia-kepler` and `nvidia-kepler-fifo` (Cargo.toml), NEITHER is in any K8_FEATS arm, and the module is declared `#[cfg(feature = "nvidia-kepler-kfbind")] pub mod kepler_fifo;` in `drivers/gpu/mod.rs` beside `kepler`/`kepler_display`/`kepler_ce`, which are all `nvidia-kepler`-gated — a Pi image never lexes any of them, which is why the tool reports 0 Pi-live. The two call sites are additionally inside `kepler::init`'s `nvidia-kepler-fifo` leg, so even a hypothetical Pi build carrying the module could not reach them. THIRD, the physical one: this is a probe rung on the 2012 rMBP's GK107 (GeForce GT 650M) — a PTOP device-info sweep and PBDMA PRI reads against NVIDIA host-engine registers on a discrete PCIe GPU, plus a BAR1 read of that GPU's channel control area. A Pi 4 has a BCM2711 with a VideoCore VI and no NVIDIA part on any bus, so there is nothing for the knob to arm there even if both reasons above were lifted. Ruled NA by the rmbp KFBIND executor (rmbp-queue GPU LADDERS; shut-out register §2 rung KF27) 2026-09-15.
UNAOS_KEPLER_KFCTXBIND    NA   --evidence, re-run at this commit and quoted verbatim: `nvidia-kepler-kfctxbind: 4 site(s), 0 Pi-live, 0 negated  [implies: nvidia-kepler, nvidia-kepler-fifo]` — the `pub mod kepler_fifo` declaration in `drivers/gpu/mod.rs` (whose gate this rung widened to `all(nvidia-kepler, nvidia-kepler-fifo, any(nvidia-kepler-kfbind, nvidia-kepler-kfctxbind))` — the `any` because KF28 deliberately does NOT imply KF27's feature, and the two parents spelled out because GATE-FC2 takes no required atom from an `any(...)` and convicted the short form as a declaration wider than its four call sites (`decl=target_arch = "x86_64" ... all-under=nvidia-kepler + nvidia-kepler-fifo -> FINDING`); both features imply both parents, so the `all(...)` admits exactly the same configurations — KEPLER-METAL-LOG.md's KF28 entry forbids flying the two rungs on the same boot, so the dependency is a RUNTIME gate and never a Cargo one), the `pub mod ctxbind` declaration inside `drivers/gpu/kepler_fifo.rs`, and the rung's TWO call sites in `drivers/gpu/kepler.rs` (phase A below KF18's CHAN_CUR/CHAN_NEXT bind and strictly pre-submit, phase B below KF27's phase B); line numbers drift, so re-run `scripts/k8-reach.py --evidence UNAOS_KEPLER_KFCTXBIND` rather than trusting them. ONE live read in the producer, arroyo, writing `_feats` (`nvidia-kepler-kfctxbind`). THREE INDEPENDENT REASONS, the same three the KFBIND row directly above establishes for this same file, with the SECOND adjusted for this feature's own implication set. FIRST: `kernel8()` builds its OWN curated feature list — `local K8_FEATS="baremetal,skip_xhci"`, extended only by its own explicit arms — and NEVER reads the `_feats` knob-mapping block, so a knob that writes `_feats` cannot change a byte of a kernel8 image. Command: `grep -n 'K8_FEATS=' unaos/arroyo` (every assignment is inside kernel8(), none from _feats). SECOND, and it would still hold if the mapping block were ever wired into kernel8: the feature implies BOTH `nvidia-kepler` and `nvidia-kepler-fifo` (Cargo.toml), NEITHER is in any K8_FEATS arm, and the module it lives in is declared beside `kepler`/`kepler_display`/`kepler_ce` in `drivers/gpu/mod.rs`, which are all `nvidia-kepler`-gated — a Pi image never lexes any of them, which is why the tool reports 0 Pi-live. Both call sites are additionally inside `kepler::init`'s `nvidia-kepler-fifo` leg, so even a hypothetical Pi build carrying the module could not reach them. THIRD, the physical one: this is a probe rung on the 2012 rMBP's GK107 (GeForce GT 650M) — a FECS falcon census, a PTOP/PBDMA PRI sweep, a PFIFO channel-table read and a BAR1 read of that GPU's instance block and channel control area, all against NVIDIA host-engine registers on a discrete PCIe GPU. A Pi 4 has a BCM2711 with a VideoCore VI and no NVIDIA part on any bus, so there is nothing for the knob to arm there even if both reasons above were lifted. Ruled NA by the rmbp KFCTXBIND executor (rmbp-queue GPU LADDERS row KFBIND-CTXBIND; shut-out register §2 rung KF28) 2026-09-15.
UNAOS_KEPLER_KDHEAD       NA   --evidence, re-run at this commit and quoted verbatim: `nvidia-kepler-kdhead: 21 site(s), 0 Pi-live, 0 negated  [implies: nvidia-kepler, nvidia-kepler-takeover]` — every one of the twenty-one is in `drivers/gpu/kepler_display.rs`: the ONE call site folded onto the existing `panel_console_resume` statement line beside BEAMX86's, the single cfg'd census-publication statement inside `beam_probe`, and nineteen items in the rung's own tail block (its constants, statics, `KdheadBlock`/`KdheadGeom`, `kdhead_publish_census`, both `kdhead_bracket` arms, `kdhead_answered`, `kdhead_decode`, `kdhead_probe` and three `const _` address asserts); line numbers drift, so re-run `scripts/k8-reach.py --evidence UNAOS_KEPLER_KDHEAD` rather than trusting them. ONE live read in the producer, arroyo, writing `_feats` (`nvidia-kepler-kdhead`). THREE INDEPENDENT REASONS, the same three the seven SHUTRESTORE rows and the two KF rows above establish for this same file family, with the SECOND strengthened by this feature's extra implication. FIRST: `kernel8()` builds its OWN curated feature list — `local K8_FEATS="baremetal,skip_xhci"`, extended only by its own explicit arms — and NEVER reads the `_feats` knob-mapping block, so a knob that writes `_feats` cannot change a byte of a kernel8 image. Command: `grep -n 'K8_FEATS=' unaos/arroyo` (every assignment is inside kernel8(), none from _feats). SECOND, and it would still hold if the mapping block were ever wired into kernel8: the feature implies BOTH `nvidia-kepler` and `nvidia-kepler-takeover` (Cargo.toml), NEITHER is in any K8_FEATS arm, and `drivers/gpu/mod.rs` declares `kepler`/`kepler_display` under `#[cfg(feature = "nvidia-kepler")]` — a Pi image never lexes the file, which is why the tool reports 0 Pi-live. The call site is additionally inside `kepler_display::takeover_display`, below that function's trace-only early return, so even a hypothetical Pi build carrying the module could not reach it. THIRD, the physical one: this is a probe rung on the 2012 rMBP's GK107 (GeForce GT 650M) — read-only MMIO reads of NVIDIA PDISPLAY `HEAD_STAT`, the EVO core-channel state and the 0x640000 method mirror on a discrete PCIe GPU. A Pi 4 has a BCM2711 with a VideoCore VI and no NVIDIA part on any bus, so there is nothing for the knob to arm there even if both reasons above were lifted. Ruled NA by the rmbp KDHEAD executor (rmbp-queue GPU LADDERS row KDHEAD; shut-out register §1 rung KD14) 2026-09-15.
